For Human Geography: Nature and Scope (Human Geography - Nature and Scope):
NCERT Class 12 Fundamentals of Human Geography (Chapter 5: Secondary Activities) classifies manufacturing by raw material:
(A) Agro-based: Sugar, cotton, rubber, tea, coffee (Correct);
(B) Animal-based: Leather, wool, silk. Pottery uses clay/earth and is mineral-based, NOT animal-based (Incorrect);
(C) Forest-based: Timber, paper, lac, turpentine (Correct);
(D) Non-ferrous mineral-based: Copper, aluminium, lead, zinc (metals without iron) (Correct).
Thus, (A), (C), and (D) only are correct.

Therefore, option (C) is the correct answer.

