Detailed Solution:
1. Crude Death Rate (CDR): Expressed as the number of deaths in a year per thousand of population (A -> II);
2. Sex Ratio (in India): Defined as the number of females per thousand males (B -> IV);
3. Population Growth Rate: Expressed as the percentage change in population over a specific period (C -> I);
4. Density of Population: Expressed as the ratio of total population to total land area, in persons per square kilometre (D -> III).
This yields (A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(III).
Hence, option (A) is the correct match.

